sec.p:
Total hardness (TH) and calcium (Ca2⁺) were measured via EDTA titration, and magnesium (Mg2⁺) was calculated by subtracting Ca2⁺ hardness from TH. Sodium (Na⁺) and potassium (K⁺) were determined using a digital flame photometer (Systronics Model 128). Bicarbonate (HCO₃⁻) was estimated by acid titration with standard H₂SO₄, and chloride (Cl⁻) by argentometric titration using AgNO₃. Fluoride (F-) was measured with an ion-selective electrode (Orion Star A214), sulphate (SO₄2⁻) by the turbidimetric method, and nitrate (NO₃⁻) using a Hach DR900 colorimeter. All reagents were prepared with double-distilled water for purity. Chemical analyses were carried out using standard protocols prescribed by the American Public Health Association (APHA)36. Analytical precision was evaluated by computing the charge balance error (CBE) using the standard charge balance equation (Eq. 1). Most samples exhibited CBE values within ± 5%, indicating acceptable accuracy.1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
